# Blacklisted due to https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues/942
The only membership state included in a gapped incremental sync is for senders in the timeline

# Sytest bug: its redaction algorithm for room versions 11 and later still keeps
# origin, membership and prev_state, which MSC2176 stopped protecting, so it
# computes other event IDs for Zendrite's version 12 events than Zendrite does
# and cannot find their auth events when Zendrite rejoins through it
Server correctly resyncs when server leaves and rejoins a room

# Flakey: as the spec asks, a join sends the user's device list to the room's
# new servers, and when the second user's update arrives after the test starts
# waiting, the test takes it for the first user's key upload
Local device key changes get to remote servers with correct prev_id

# Flakey: notification counts are worked out after the event reaches /sync, so
# the sync after the one with the new event can carry the room with only its
# new unread_notifications, which the test expects to be empty
The only membership state included in an incremental sync is for senders in the timeline

# Zendrite answers M_NOT_FOUND here, as the spec allows for /state_ids, and both pass with --room-version 10.
# In room version 12 (the Sytest default) Sytest's redaction keeps origin and prev_state, which room version 11 dropped.
# Zendrite's events still carry both fields, so Sytest computes the wrong event IDs and fails before the request.
/state returns M_NOT_FOUND for an outlier
/state_ids returns M_NOT_FOUND for an outlier

# this is a silly restriction as it basically stops servers from communicating, so we relax it
# see https://github.com/element-hq/synapse/issues/7543
Server rejects invalid JSON in a version 6 room
